Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 13:37:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Pad the super-slow-motion encoder input buffer to eliminate
 the 960fps green line artifact

The 1080p/960fps slow-motion post-processor (XiaomiAlgoEncoderAsync) copies a tightly packed NV21 frame (1920x1080x1.5 = 3,110,400 B) into a stride-aligned MediaCodec input buffer (3,125,760 B) and queues it without initialising the 15,360 B tail, which decodes as a green band on the left edge after rotation.

EncoderInputFix.padInputTail repeats the last chroma row into that tail immediately before ByteBuffer.put(); it returns the array unchanged when the sizes already match, so every other capture mode keeps its exact behaviour.

Verified on device: logcat shows padInputTail 3110400 -> 3125760 and a fresh 960fps capture contains 0 green pixels per frame against 39,691 in the pre-fix capture (identical VLC paused-frame pixel count).

Signed-off-by: Sachin <sachinbarange86@gmail.com>
